      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A case of angina pectoris worsened by prazosin is presented. Since a hypertensive population includes many patients with known or occult coronary artery disease, physicians should use prazosin cautiously in this subgroup, particularly when beta-adrenergic antagonists cannot be used concurrently."},
